    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ratumēna Porta</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ratumen-na</span></b> ). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a gate at Rome</i>, which, acc. to
			Festus, derived its name from an Etruscan youth, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				275</span></i> Müll.; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 42,
				65, § 161</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sol. 45,
			15</span></i> (in Plut. Public. 13, written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥατουμένα</span>).</div>
